# Build config for the single-origin reverse-proxy deployment.
# Read by `npm run build:remote` (vite build --mode remote).
#
# `same-origin` tells the dashboard to resolve the API against window.location
# instead of a baked-in address, so ONE build is correct everywhere it is served:
# https://cronsole.example.com through the tunnel and http://localhost:8080 on the
# proxy locally. That is what removes the per-device "API origin" override.
#
# SINCE 2026-08-17 THIS FILE IS BELT-AND-BRACES, NOT THE MECHANISM. Every
# production build now defaults to same-origin on its own (`FALLBACK_API_ORIGIN`
# in src/api.ts folds on `import.meta.env.DEV`), so `npm run build` and
# `npm run build:remote` produce the same correct bundle. The mode is kept
# because runbooks, docs and muscle memory all name it, and because stating the
# intent explicitly is still worth something — but correctness no longer depends
# on anyone remembering it.
#
# This file previously warned NOT to use same-origin for a normal local build,
# on the reasoning that the API is on :3000 and the page on :7373. That reasoning
# was about the DEV SERVER, which never reads `dist` at all — and the warning made
# `npm run build` look like the safe default when it was the one that silently
# broke phone access (troubleshooting #63, twice). The dev server keeps its
# :3000 default through the DEV branch in the code, not through an env file.
#
# Nothing secret goes in this file; VITE_* values are compiled into the bundle
# and served to every visitor.
VITE_API_URL=same-origin
